Refreshed for full syntax hygiene. This seed had gone stale alongside the native
ones, and because it is the FALLBACK -- `select_stage0` reaches for it exactly
when a platform's native seed cannot compile the tree -- both being stale left
Linux CI with no way to bootstrap at all ("WASM stage0 cannot compile the current
source tree"). The Linux native seeds are still pre-migration; that job now
bootstraps through this file, which is what it is for.

Verified: COIL_FORCE_WASM_STAGE0=1 scripts/dev.py build reaches the stage2/stage3
fixed point. Building it also needed three host imports the translated module had
started calling -- atexit, isatty, unsetenv -- added to src/bootstrap/runtime.c to
match run-coil-wasm.mjs, which already had all three.
